1	1	"[[\\"Whole Milk\\",360],[\\"Heavy Cream\\",360],[\\"Skimmed Milk Powder\\",55],[\\"Egg Yolk\\",36],[\\"Sucrose\\",70],[\\"Dextrose\\",25],[\\"Invert Sugar\\",15],[\\"Locust Bean Gum\\",0.8],[\\"Guar Gum\\",0.4],[\\"Lambda Carrageenan\\",0.2],[\\"Salt\\",0.7]]"	[Underbelly's Standard Base](https://under-belly.org/basic-ice-cream-recipe-examples/) recipe,\nposted 2016-05-25, visited 2026-05-7.\n\n'Whole Milk' is quoted as 3.3%, which I assume is 3.25% rounded up, consistent with Sci-Cream's\ndefinition. 'Heavy Cream' is quoted as 36%, consistent with Sci-Cream's definition. The 'Egg Yolk'\namount is a whole multiple of 18g large egg yolks. The stabilizers are the 4:2:1 'Underbelly General\nPurpose Stabilizer Blend', total 1.4g.\n\nThe 15g of 'Invert Sugar' can be replaced by 6g each of 'Dextrose' and 'Fructose', as per\n[this](https://under-belly.org/basic-ice-cream-recipe-examples/#comment-709) and\n[this](https://under-belly.org/basic-ice-cream-recipe-examples/#comment-12) comment, which is much\neasier to work with.	\N	\N	\N	2026-08-16 04:50:54.090484	\N
2	1	"[[\\"Whole Milk\\",360],[\\"Heavy Cream\\",360],[\\"Skimmed Milk Powder\\",15],[\\"Egg Yolk\\",108],[\\"Sucrose\\",75],[\\"Dextrose\\",35],[\\"Invert Sugar\\",15],[\\"Locust Bean Gum\\",0.6],[\\"Guar Gum\\",0.3],[\\"Lambda Carrageenan\\",0.15],[\\"Salt\\",0.7]]"	[Underbelly's French Variation](https://under-belly.org/basic-ice-cream-recipe-examples/) recipe,\nposted 2016-05-25, visited 2026-05-7.\n\n'Whole Milk' is quoted as 3.3%, which I assume is 3.25% rounded up, consistent with Sci-Cream's\ndefinition. 'Heavy Cream' is quoted as 36%, consistent with Sci-Cream's definition. The 'Egg Yolk'\namount is a whole multiple of 18g large egg yolks. The stabilizers are the 4:2:1 'Underbelly General\nPurpose Stabilizer Blend', total 1.05g.\n\nThe 15g of 'Invert Sugar' can be replaced by 6g each of 'Dextrose' and 'Fructose', as per\n[this](https://under-belly.org/basic-ice-cream-recipe-examples/#comment-709) and\n[this](https://under-belly.org/basic-ice-cream-recipe-examples/#comment-12) comment, which is much\neasier to work with.	\N	\N	\N	2026-08-16 04:50:54.093074	\N
3	1	"[[\\"Whole Milk\\",480],[\\"Heavy Cream\\",240],[\\"Skimmed Milk Powder\\",85],[\\"Sucrose\\",70],[\\"Dextrose\\",30],[\\"Invert Sugar\\",15],[\\"Soy Lecithin\\",2],[\\"Locust Bean Gum\\",0.8],[\\"Guar Gum\\",0.6],[\\"Lambda Carrageenan\\",0.4],[\\"Salt\\",0.7]]"	[Underbelly's Light Variation](https://under-belly.org/basic-ice-cream-recipe-examples/) recipe,\nposted 2016-05-25, visited 2026-05-7.\n\n'Whole Milk' is quoted as 3.3%, which I assume is 3.25% rounded up, consistent with Sci-Cream's\ndefinition. 'Heavy Cream' is quoted as 36%, consistent with Sci-Cream's definition. The stabilizers\nare a 4:3:2 blend, total 1.8g, and 2g of 'Soy Lecithin'. This is inconsistent with 'Underbelly\nEggless Ice Cream Stabilizer Blend', which uses a 4:2:1 blend, and 4 'Soy Lecithin'. It's also\ninconsistent with the 2.1g of stabilizers in the composition table, and with the stated 4.5g of 'Soy\nLecithin' in the discussion. The stabilizer blends were both ostensibly edited on 2018-10, but they\nare inconsistent with each other.\n\nThe 15g of 'Invert Sugar' can be replaced by 6g each of 'Dextrose' and 'Fructose', as per\n[this](https://under-belly.org/basic-ice-cream-recipe-examples/#comment-709) and\n[this](https://under-belly.org/basic-ice-cream-recipe-examples/#comment-12) comment, which is much\neasier to work with.	\N	\N	\N	2026-08-16 04:50:54.095612	\N
4	1	"[[\\"Whole Milk\\",470],[\\"Heavy Cream\\",240],[\\"Cocoa Powder, 22% Fat\\",70],[\\"70% Dark Chocolate\\",90],[\\"Dextrose\\",84],[\\"Fructose\\",29],[\\"Soy Lecithin\\",2],[\\"Locust Bean Gum\\",0.8],[\\"Guar Gum\\",0.6],[\\"Lambda Carrageenan\\",0.4],[\\"Salt\\",1.2],[\\"Vanilla Extract\\",10]]"	[Underbelly's "Double Origin" Chocolate Ice\nCream](https://under-belly.org/ice-cream-flavor-chocolate/) recipe, posted 2018-09-25, visited\n2026-06-16.\n\nCocoa powder is assumed to be 22% fat, typical of the brands mentioned, e.g. Valrhona, and agrees\nwith the stated total fat content. Chocolate is assumed to be 70% dark chocolate, in the middle of\nthe stated 67-72% range. The stabilizers are a 4:3:2 blend, total 1.8g, and 2g of 'Soy Lecithin' -\nthis does not match any of Underbelly's listed stabilizer blends, though it does match the 'Light\nVariation' blend. The resulting composition agrees with the stated 'Analysis' - except POD and PAC.	\N	\N	\N	2026-08-16 04:50:54.098041	\N
5	1	"[[\\"Whole Milk\\",395],[\\"Heavy Cream\\",310],[\\"Skimmed Milk Powder\\",30],[\\"Cocoa Powder, 17% Fat\\",110],[\\"Sucrose\\",80],[\\"Dextrose\\",50],[\\"Fructose\\",12],[\\"Soy Lecithin\\",2],[\\"Locust Bean Gum\\",0.8],[\\"Guar Gum\\",0.6],[\\"Lambda Carrageenan\\",0.4],[\\"Salt\\",1.2],[\\"Vanilla Extract\\",10]]"	[Underbelly's Single Origin Cocoa Ice Cream](https://under-belly.org/ice-cream-flavor-chocolate/)\nrecipe, posted 2018-09-25, visited 2026-06-16.\n\nCocoa powder is taken as 17% fat, in the middle of the stated 15-20% range. The stabilizers are a\n4:3:2 blend, total 1.8g, and 2g of 'Soy Lecithin' - this does not match any of Underbelly's listed\nstabilizer blends, though it does match the 'Light Variation' blend. The resulting composition\nagrees with the stated 'Analysis'.	\N	\N	\N	2026-08-16 04:50:54.100496	\N
6	1	"[[\\"Whole Milk\\",360],[\\"Heavy Cream\\",360],[\\"Skimmed Milk Powder\\",55],[\\"Egg Yolk\\",36],[\\"Sucrose\\",70],[\\"Invert Sugar\\",5],[\\"Honey\\",7],[\\"Locust Bean Gum\\",1],[\\"Guar Gum\\",0.4],[\\"Lambda Carrageenan\\",0.2],[\\"Salt\\",0.7],[\\"Grand Marnier\\",60]]"	[Underbelly's Grand Marnier Ice Cream](https://under-belly.org/booze-flavored-ice-cream/) recipe,\nposted 2016-12-16, visited 2026-06-21.\n\nThe recipe specifies 'Chestnut Honey'. The stabilizers are a unique 5:2:1 blend, total 1.6g	\N	\N	\N	2026-08-16 04:50:54.103004	\N
7	1	"[[\\"Whole Milk\\",340],[\\"Heavy Cream\\",360],[\\"Skimmed Milk Powder\\",55],[\\"Egg Yolk\\",36],[\\"Sucrose\\",85],[\\"Invert Sugar\\",12],[\\"Locust Bean Gum\\",0.8],[\\"Guar Gum\\",0.4],[\\"Lambda Carrageenan\\",0.2],[\\"Salt\\",1],[\\"Lemon Zest\\",4],[\\"Lemon Juice\\",24],[\\"Bourbon Whiskey\\",65],[\\"Angostura Aromatic Bitters\\",2],[\\"Fresh Spearmint\\",12],[\\"Peppermint Essential Oil\\",0.1]]"	[Underbelly's Bourbon Smash Ice Cream](https://under-belly.org/booze-flavored-ice-cream/) recipe,\nposted 2016-12-16, visited 2026-06-21.\n\nThe stabilizers are the 4:2:1 'Underbelly General Purpose Stabilizer Blend', total 1.4g. 'Lemon\nZest' and 'Fresh Spearmint' may only partially contribute to the composition, depending on the\npreparation, e.g. if the mint is infused rather than blended into the mix. 'Bourbon' is listed as\n43%, which Sci-Cream's 'Bourbon Whiskey' matches, but other bourbons can range from 40-45% ABV; one\ncan substitute in 'X% ABV Spirit' to match the specific bourbon used. The recipe states "very fresh\nmint leaves" and "mint essential oil" without specifying a variety - spearmint is commonly used in\ncocktails, and peppermint essential oil is most common.	\N	\N	\N	2026-08-16 04:50:54.10552	\N
8	1	"[[\\"Double Cream\\",417],[\\"Skim Milk\\",319],[\\"Skimmed Milk Powder\\",46],[\\"Sucrose\\",140],[\\"Egg Yolk\\",78],[\\"Cocoa Powder, 17% Fat\\",30],[\\"70% Dark Chocolate\\",50],[\\"Salt\\",3],[\\"Vanilla Extract\\",5],[\\"Instant Coffee\\",1]]"	[Ice Cream Science's Chocolate Ice\nCream](https://www.icecreamscience.com/blog/chocolate-ice-cream-recipe) recipe, visited 2026-07-07.\n\nThe preparation instructions ask for the dairy, sugar, and egg yolk mix to be reduced by 15%, which\nworks out to 150g of water evaporated. The recipe states '1 tsp vanilla extract', which is ~5g. The\nrecipe asks for '3g whole coffee beans' to be heated with the mix and then strained out. This has a\nnegligible effect on the mix composition; I suspect that it's equivalent to a tiny amount of instant\ncoffee, so I have modeled it as 1g of instant coffee. The recipe does not specify a fat content for\nthe cocoa powder; 17% fat is a common mid-range value.	\N	\N	\N	2026-08-16 04:50:54.107897	\N
