16	1	"[[\\"Horizon Organic Heavy Whipping Cream\\",183],[\\"Organic Valley Organic Whole Milk\\",179],[\\"Carnation Sweetened Condensed Milk (US)\\",165]]"	[Ice Cream Science's Ninja Creami NC301 Easy No-Cook Tres Leches\n(US)](https://www.icecreamscience.com/blog/ninja-creami-nc30-easy-no-cook-tres-leches-recipe)\nrecipe, visited 2026-07-06.\n\nSci-Cream's composition of the ingredients used in the recipe do not agree with Ice Cream Science's\ncomposition - milk is 3.23% vs 3.6% fat, cream is 33.4% vs 32.4% fat, and most importantly,\nsweetened condensed milk is 46% vs ~58% sucrose. As a result, the mix composition differs\nsignificantly from Ice Cream Science's composition, with total solids 41.1% vs 46.34%, MSNF 10.9% vs\n12.16%, fat 15.5% vs 16.02%, and sucrose 14.5% vs 18.15%. This is the US version of the recipe; see\n"Ninja Creami NC301 Easy No-Cook Tres Leches (UK)" for the UK version. This is a no-cook recipe\nintended to be made using the Ninja Creami NC301 ice cream maker; I am not sure how it would perform\nin a standard ice cream maker.	\N	\N	\N	2026-08-16 04:50:54.12923	\N
